KIM (Korea Meteorological Administration)
-----------------------------------------
Charts labelled "KIM global" / "KIM regional" are derived from the Korean Integrated Model (KIM) forecasts
downloaded from the KMA API Hub (https://apihub.kma.go.kr/).
Source: Korea Meteorological Administration (기상청). Licence: Korea Open Government License (KOGL, 공공누리)
Type 1 - attribution required (https://www.kogl.or.kr/info/licenseType1.do).
Modifications: regional fields interpolated from the 3 km Lambert grid to a 0.05 deg lat/lon grid; global
fields cropped; derived quantities computed; charts rendered. Not an official KMA product.


Climate lines on the ensemble graphs
------------------------------------
500 hPa height and 850 hPa temperature: ERA5 1990-2019 6-hourly climatology as published by WeatherBench2
(https://storage.googleapis.com/weatherbench2/), interpolated to the graph points.
Contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information (ERA5, Hersbach et al. 2020).
Neither the European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use of this information.
2 m temperature: KMA ASOS daily climatological normals (평년값, 1991-2020; Daegu 1981-2010) from the KMA API Hub.
Source: Korea Meteorological Administration (기상청), KOGL Type 1 - attribution required. Not an official KMA product.
